Subject: NUL-terminate the frame that the fuzzy superblock search scans
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

iso9660_ifs_fuzzy_read_superblock looks for "CD001" with strstr in a
frame buffer that is exactly CDIO_CD_FRAMESIZE_RAW bytes. A raw 2352-byte
read fills it completely, so strstr ran past the end. Fil-C stopped
isofuzzy there (check_fuzzyiso.sh). Keep one more zero byte after the
frame.

--- a/lib/iso9660/iso9660_fs.c
+++ b/lib/iso9660/iso9660_fs.c
@@ -579,7 +579,8 @@
 
       for (k=0; k < 3; k++) {
 	char *p, *q;
-	char frame[CDIO_CD_FRAMESIZE_RAW] = {'\0',};
+	/* One extra NUL so that strstr below stays inside the frame. */
+	char frame[CDIO_CD_FRAMESIZE_RAW + 1] = {'\0',};
 	p_iso->i_framesize = framesizes[k];
 	p_iso->i_datastart = (ISO_BLOCKSIZE == framesizes[k]) ?
 			      0 : CDIO_CD_SYNC_SIZE;
